{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question","id":959268,"title":"Vampires and space travel question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-28T08:37:17-07:00","id":959268,"title":"Vampires and space travel question","content":"Ok so me and a player were talking about how much blood it would take for a kindred to travel 4 light years on a space craft traveling 25 miles per second. <br /> <br /> So lets say their is a planet 4 lights away that holds aliens life and we wanted to send a kindred because they can live forever how much blood would that kindred need to survive the trip ?<br /> <br /> So and adult human holds around 10 pints of blood <br /> <br /> when a kindred drinks a person blood in game 1 point of Vitae equals 1 lethal point of damage. <br /> <br /> The average human has only has 7 health in game so we know its not 1 to 1. So after doing a bit of googling I found that most humans die after losing more then 40% of blood. Being most kindred only drink enough to leave a human woozy. So lets say that 1 and half pints per health level giving us a total of 10.5 pints in a normal adult human in the world of darkness. So that means a kindred can live on around 1 and half pints of blood per day giving them a single Vitae. So 29,800 years to days gives us a grand total of 10877000 days. Giving us a grand total of 16,315,500 pints of blood or 2,039,437.5 Gallons or 64224.733 Tons and that's to just get their. We would need to double these numbers to figure out how much a round trip is. <br /> <br /> Did I do the math right ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:46:32-07:00","id":959274,"title":"","content":"No feeding on humans would be required. The vampire goes into voluntary torpor. They wake up when they arrive at their destination and can feed off the livestock brought along for the colony of humans who accompanied him on the trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:03:11-07:00","id":959290,"title":"","content":"As it's been explained several times, Vitae isn't a direct translation of blood volume leaving the human recipient and into the vampire. It's a measure of life-force. 4 points of vitae could be as little as 4 sips off a vein. Contrast with how Strix get the same sustenance, but taken out of their victim's breath.<br /> <br /> Vampires can drain people completely of their life-force, and it wouldn't look like exsaguination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:42:21-07:00","id":959307,"title":"","content":"Stored blood is also pretty useless, if you were planning on storing it on a space ship or something. It's life energy in the blood they're feeding on. Blood loses any usefulness really quick outside a living body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cold blood from a corpse or kept outside the body for<br /> more than a few minutes (but no more than a night) is far<br /> less satisfying. To gain a single point of Vitae, a vampire must<br /> consume as many pints of this blood as her Blood Potency times<br /> two. Technologically stored blood, for example in refrigerated<br /> plasma bags, is similarly unpalatable to potent Kindred. </div> </div> </div>&quot;No more than a single night&quot; suggests that you couldn't just keep a tank of blood on a ship to feed the vampire. It'd lose all potency long before they arrived. Torpor is the best bet, though finding food at the other end...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10:36:47-07:00","id":959326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959307#post959307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stored blood is also pretty useless, if you were planning on storing it on a space ship or something. It's life energy in the blood they're feeding on. Blood loses any usefulness really quick outside a living body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;No more than a single night&amp;quot; suggests that you couldn't just keep a tank of blood on a ship to feed the vampire. It'd lose all potency long before they arrived. Torpor is the best bet, though finding food at the other end...</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that quote as meaning that technologically stored blood is equivalent to blood that has been out of the body for more than a few minutes but less than a full night. Either way though, yeah, that's <i>way</i> more blood than would be feasible to transport on a four-year space expedition. It costs about 10,000 dollars per pound just to get something to Mars, which is only about 6-8 months away with current technology. Torpor is a much better bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:05:15-07:00","id":959338,"title":"","content":"Right, yes. I keep forgetting the last sentence. It can be stored, but that is a lot of blood. Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:32:46-07:00","id":959349,"title":"","content":"Yeah, vampires with BP more than 1 require more weight in stores blood than humans require weight in food and water per day when they're active. To actually save on fuel you'd need them in torpor, or to have fresh sources of blood, which will themselves require food and water to sustain.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, though, sending a torpid vamp would mean there would be no need to regulate the temperature or the O2 and CO2 levels in the vehicle, which means you don't need to waste weight limit on air conditioning and filtration equipment. And with no oxygen there'd be no risk of fire in the cabin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-28-2016, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:45:09-07:00","id":959528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959274#post959274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No feeding on humans would be required. The vampire goes into voluntary torpor. They wake up when they arrive at their destination and can feed off the livestock brought along for the colony of humans who accompanied him on the trip.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> Well we were imaging a single kindred being sent not a group of beings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:46:31-07:00","id":959529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959349#post959349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, vampires with BP more than 1 require more weight in stores blood than humans require weight in food and water per day when they're active. To actually save on fuel you'd need them in torpor, or to have fresh sources of blood, which will themselves require food and water to sustain.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, though, sending a torpid vamp would mean there would be no need to regulate the temperature or the O2 and CO2 levels in the vehicle, which means you don't need to waste weight limit on air conditioning and filtration equipment. And with no oxygen there'd be no risk of fire in the cabin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a good point I did not think about the O2 and CO2 thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:48:58-07:00","id":959568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959528#post959528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'<br /> Well we were imaging a single kindred being sent not a group of beings</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then you have this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwmA6EJs-zc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwmA6EJs-zc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwmA6EJs-zc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwmA6EJs-zc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tzRFARUa3c4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tzRFARUa3c4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tzRFARUa3c4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tzRFARUa3c4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T20:01:41-07:00","id":959637,"title":"","content":"The hard part is when is it night and when is it day? I mean there is no planet between you and the sun so when you start it will be day all the time (day sleep 24x7). I assume once you get far enough away, it will be night all the time. At that point, you won't need to rouse yourself from sleep as the night never ends so you never suffer from daysleep.. You may end up never having to spend blood as you only spend it to wake up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T20:42:03-07:00","id":959647,"title":"","content":"Yeah, space travel gets really weird in CofD. How do you determine night and day in space? Does any star's light cause aggravated damage to vampires, or only Sol's? Do werewolves born on other planets get Auspices based on Luna's phases, or the phases of the moons of their native planets? Or do they not get Auspices at all? Do other planets have their own Gauntlets? Does space have a Gauntlet? Do intelligent alien species have their own Temenos? es it connect to the Anima Mundi? Does it have a different Primordial Dream? Can Beasts from Earth Lair there? It's a huge headache and one of the reasons I've always been kind of iffy about Infinite Macabre. So much of CofD is built assuming all the characters live on and stay on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T00:33:58-07:00","id":959703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959637#post959637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard part is when is it night and when is it day? I mean there is no planet between you and the sun so when you start it will be day all the time (day sleep 24x7). I assume once you get far enough away, it will be night all the time. At that point, you won't need to rouse yourself from sleep as the night never ends so you never suffer from daysleep.. You may end up never having to spend blood as you only spend it to wake up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That makes me wonder what happens with a vampire goes to another part of the world. Do they get jet lagged or do they automatically sync up to the date night cycle of their location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T03:18:14-07:00","id":959732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959703#post959703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That makes me wonder what happens with a vampire goes to another part of the world. Do they get jet lagged or do they automatically sync up to the date night cycle of their location.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always run it as they sync up automatically to the local sun-cycle. So the poles during summer would be a very long sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T03:39:27-07:00","id":959737,"title":"","content":"It might be worth noting that there is a book for this. One of the MIrrors supplements covers space opera, if I remember correctly. Though I don't know how many of these issues, if any, are covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T04:00:07-07:00","id":959743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959268-vampires-and-space-travel-question?p=959737#post959737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be worth noting that there is a book for this. One of the MIrrors supplements covers space opera, if I remember correctly. Though I don't know how many of these issues, if any, are covered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty certain it covers all of them but it doesn't give a definitive answer and just gives ideas for what the ST can do.<br /> <br /> Edit: the book is mirrors: infinite macabre by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6365,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","user":"Fumus","date":". 08-29-2016, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T06:49:39-07:00","id":959784,"title":"","content":"Topor vampire at beginning of the trip. 'Technologically store' twenty pts of blood. Wait travel time. Vampire wakes up. Needs BP*2 pts of blood. Drinks tank. Elder adapts to new 'era' hopefully allowing consumption of the natives. Optional: Send a Venture, planet brought to heel. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}